UPDATE companies SET description='Malama Solar is a locally owned and operated solar installation company based in Honolulu, Hawaii. Founders Chris and Rachel Ah Sue formed the company with a mission rooted in the Hawaiian value of Mālama ''Āina—caring for the land so it cares for you. Rachel, born and raised on O''ahu, and Chris, who moved to the islands after college, started the business to provide a transparent, quality-driven alternative in Hawaii''s residential solar market.

The company designs and installs custom photovoltaic systems for homeowners on Oahu and the Big Island, managing every step from initial energy-usage analysis and system design through permitting, HOA approvals, financing coordination, and final installation. Installation crews typically complete the physical work in about two days, with the overall process taking six to eight weeks after a customer commits. Malama Solar partners with manufacturers, distributors, and financial institutions to supply panels, modular battery storage, and financing options tailored to each household.

The firm serves residential customers across Hawaii, with recent projects cited in Kona, Kapolei, and Ewa Beach. Its primary industry is residential solar installation and energy storage, helping homeowners reduce reliance on utility power amid rising electricity rates.

Malama Solar says it was founded to be different—emphasizing a five-step process that prioritizes transparency, local crew members who share community ties, and ongoing customer support after the system is powered on.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system consultation and energy-usage analysis", "Custom system design and engineering", "Permitting and HOA approval management", "Solar panel installation", "Energy storage (battery) installation", "Financing coordination with partner institutions", "Post-installation customer service and support"], "industries": ["Residential solar installation", "Renewable energy", "Energy storage"], "materials": ["Solar panels (various manufacturers)", "Modular battery storage systems"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "6-8 weeks for full system installation after commitment (sometimes as soon as 3 weeks); physical installation takes about 2 days", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Five-step process from consultation to post-installation support", "Local installation crews on Oahu and Big Island", "Handles all permitting, HOA approvals, and financing paperwork", "Partners with manufacturers and financial institutions for panels, storage, and financing", "Founded on Hawaiian value of M\u0101lama ''\u0100ina (care for the land)"], "facts_used": ["Locally owned and operated solar company in Hawaii -> /", "Founders Chris and Rachel Ah Sue formed the company -> /about-us", "Rachel born and raised on O''ahu, Chris moved to O''ahu after college -> /about-us", "5-step process: Consult, Design, Permits, Installation, Power on the Savings -> /services", "Installation typically takes 6-8 weeks after commitment, sometimes as soon as 3 weeks; installation itself about 2 days -> /services", "Partners with manufacturers, distributors, and financial institutions for panels, energy storage, and financing -> /", "Serves residential customers on Oahu and Big Island -> /", "Customer examples in Kona, Kapo