UPDATE companies SET description='Malloy Electric traces its roots to 1945, when Emmett and Mary Malloy opened a modest motor repair and electric construction shop in downtown Sioux Falls, South Dakota. The business expanded in 1971 under Garry and Dianne Jacobson, who added retail sales of motors, electrical equipment, and power transmission components. Today the company operates eight Centers of Excellence across a six-state footprint—South Dakota, North Dakota, Nebraska, Iowa, Wyoming, and Montana—with its 150,000-square-foot National Operations Center in Sioux Falls serving as headquarters.

The company provides full-lifecycle services for industrial rotating and control equipment. Its motor repair centers handle units from fractional horsepower through 15,000 HP, following EASA AR100 standards, and its machine shops support gearbox rebuilds covering helical, bevel, worm, planetary, and cycloidal reducers. Malloy also designs and builds UL508A-certified custom control panels, motor control centers, and VFD panels, and offers medium-voltage drive system installation up to 15 kV. The Sioux Falls facility houses a 70,000-pound lifting capacity, an 8-foot VPI tank, and static motor analyzers capable of testing to 30 kV. The company stocks more than 5,000 motors ranging from 1/125 HP to over 2,000 HP.

Malloy serves industrial plants, utilities, electric cooperatives, mines, and processors throughout the northern plains and mountain west. Customers rely on its 24/7 field service dispatched from local centers for motor rewinds, gearbox repairs, VFD commissioning, and predictive maintenance programs that include vibration analysis, thermography, and partial discharge testing.

The firm emphasizes problem-solving over parts replacement, continuous investment in capability (such as laser cladding and facility modernization), proximity to customers for rapid response, documented quality records with warranties, and a commitment to long-term relationships—principles that have sustained eight decades of continuous operation.', certifications=ARRAY['EASA AR100','UL508A','UL698A']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Motor repair and rewind (up to 15,000 HP)", "New motor sales (fractional to 2,000+ HP)", "Gearbox rebuild and repair (parallel shaft helical, bevel helical, worm, planetary, cycloidal, shaft-mounted)", "Gearbox sales (authorized Martin, Timken, SEW Eurodrive)", "VFD selection, installation, commissioning, field service (low voltage, medium voltage NPC, CHB, LCI topologies)", "Custom UL508A control panel design and manufacture (MCCs, VFD panels, PLC panels, HVAC, pump, hazardous location)", "UL698A hazardous location panel fabrication", "Transformer installation, service, testing", "Medium voltage drive system installation, commissioning, service", "Predictive maintenance (vibration analysis, thermography, oil analysis, motor current signature analysis, partial discharge testing)", "Static motor/generator testing (Baker D12R up to 12kV, Baker D12R with PP185D up to 30kV, PdMA MCE up to 5kV)", "Core loss testing", "Thermal imaging analysis", "UL explosion proof motor recertification", "Machining services", "Laser cladding", "Bearing protection services (AEGIS shaft grounding ring installation, shaft voltage testing, bearing cutting/inspection)", "Energy savings audits", "Motor retrofits with adapter bases", "70,000 lb lifting capability", "8'' VPI tank", "Load testing", "Full voltage testing to 7.2 kV"], "industries": ["Industrial plants", "Utilities", "Electric cooperatives", "Mines", "Processors", "Heavy industry"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Baker D12R static motor analyzer", "Baker D12R with PP185D power pack (30 kV capability)", "PdMA MCE motor circuit evaluator", "8-foot VPI tank", "70,000 lb lifting capacity", "Load test equipment", "Laser cladding system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Problem-solving engineering approach rather than simple parts substitution", "Continuous investment in capability (150,000 sq ft National Operations Center, laser cladding, modernized Centers of Excellence)", "Eight Centers of Excellence across six states enabling fast local response", "Documented quality records and warranties on every job", "Eight decades of continuous operation since 1945"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1945 by Emmett and Mary Malloy in Sioux Falls, SD -> /about", "Garry and Dianne Jacobson took helm in 1971 -> /about", "Eight Centers of Excellence across six states (SD, ND, NE, IA, WY, MT) -> /about", "150,000 sq ft National Operations Center in Sioux Falls -> /about", "Motor repair up to 15,000 HP following EASA AR100 -> /about", "Gearbox rebuild covering helical, bevel, worm, planetary, cycloidal -> /about", "VFD service for low voltage and medium voltage (NPC, CHB, LCI) -> /about", "Custom UL508A control panels and UL698A hazardous location -> /about", "Transformer services and medium voltage drive systems -> /about", "Predictive maintenance: vibration, thermography, oil analysis, MCSA, partial discharge -> /about", "Over 5,000 motors in stock from 1/125 HP to 2,000+ HP -> /services", "70,000 lb lifting capability, 8'' VPI tank, load testing -> /services", "Baker D12R and Baker D12R with PP185D (30 kV) static analyzers -> /services", "PdMA MCE analyzer up to 5 kV -> /services", "Authorized motor brands: ABB, Siemens, WEG, Regal Beloit, Toshiba -> /about", "Authorized gearbox brands: Martin, Timken, SEW Eurodrive -> /about", "Authorized VFD brands: ABB, Toshiba, Fuji -> /about", "24/7 service availability -> /", "Laser cladding capability -> /about", "AEGIS shaft grounding ring installation -> /services"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "m