UPDATE companies SET description='Marshfield Furniture has been manufacturing handcrafted upholstered furniture in Marshfield, Wisconsin since 1944. The company was founded as a domestic producer of residential furniture and continues to operate from its original Midwestern location.

The company produces living room, dining room, and bedroom collections that are handcrafted to order. Its manufacturing process combines wood frame construction with upholstery, offering customers a choice of over 75 frame styles and more than 500 fabric options, plus 48 leather selections. Each piece is built as a custom order rather than held in finished‑goods inventory, allowing retailers to specify configurations that match regional demand.

Its business-to-business customers are independent furniture stores and regional chains that carry the brand’s transitional, modern, and rustic lodge collections. The company positions itself as a partner to those retailers, providing unique collections and special‑order capabilities rather than commodity stock.

