UPDATE companies SET description='Maui Industrial Metal Fabricators has operated from Puunene, Hawaii since 1990. The locally owned shop was founded to serve Maui County with custom metal fabrication and steel supply.

The company provides custom metal fabrication, structural steel, and a range of steel materials including hot rolled steel, galvanized steel, aluminum, and stainless steel. Certified welders handle projects of any size, from simple fabrications to complex assemblies, and the firm also stocks sheets, plates, beams, and bars for immediate sale.

Customers include architects, contractors, and builders across Maui County who rely on the shop for construction and industrial projects. The business works closely with design professionals to supply fabricated and raw steel that fits project specifications.

Maui Industrial Metal Fabricators was recognized as one of Hawaii''s Fastest 50 in 1999 and holds an A+ rating from the Better Business Bureau. The company emphasizes customer satisfaction, offers financing on contract jobs, and promotes a "no job too big or too small" approach.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom metal fabrication", "Structural steel fabrication", "Steel material supply", "Certified welding"], "industries": ["Construction", "Architecture", "General Contracting", "Building Construction"], "materials": ["Hot Rolled Steel", "Galvanized Steel", "Aluminum", "Stainless Steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Certified welders on staff", "No job too big or too small", "A+ Better Business Bureau rating", "Hawaii''s Fastest 50 honoree (1999)", "Financing available on contract jobs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1990 -> /", "Located in Puunene, Hawaii -> /", "Locally owned business -> /", "Certified welders -> /", "Materials: Hot Rolled Steel, Galvanized Steel, Aluminum, Stainless Steel -> /", "Services: custom fabrication, structural steel, steel material supply -> /", "Industries: construction, architects, contractors, builders -> /", "Hawaii''s Fastest 50 1999 -> /", "BBB A+ rating -> /", "Financing options on contract jobs -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "specializes in steel fabrication, structural steel, and steel sales", "founded_year": "1990", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='maui-industrial-metal-fabricators' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='McFee Medical Technologies operates from Battle Creek, Michigan, where it was founded in 1997 as one of the first companies to offer rental equipment for vitrectomy surgery recovery. The business began by addressing the need for comfortable face-down positioning during the critical post-operative period for retinal and macular procedures.

The company designs, manufactures, and rents a range of proprietary recovery devices, including the patented MajicView Mirror and Rollover Alarm, as well as disposable face-down supports, travel cushions, and prone sleeping pillows. It provides customized equipment packages tailored to individual body types and activities, supplemented by free phone consultations, insurance claim assistance, setup videos, and same-day order processing for ground shipping.

McFee serves patients recovering from vitrectomy surgery across the United States, with testimonials from individuals in Wisconsin, Nevada, Vermont, Texas, Florida, Missouri, and Arkansas. Ophthalmologists and retinal specialists also refer patients through a dedicated physician portal, relying on the equipment to support compliance with face-down positioning requirements that typically last one to two weeks.

